Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:28:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] windows: rebase-snap and cpu-template-helper build on Windows

rebase-snap's root declares wick-std as snapshot-editor's does (patch
0017), for std::os::unix's AsRawFd; sendfile64 and SEEK_DATA/SEEK_HOLE come
from wick's POSIX layer. cpu-template-helper's build script links its mock
x86_64 kernel (a _start that spins) with gcc, which makes no Linux ELF on a
Windows host: there the script writes that ELF itself, one loadable segment
at gcc's static address with `jmp .`. Upstream's integration tests run both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
